    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45648" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφελίσσω</span></b>  (only in form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπε</span></b> ( <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι</span></b> )
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ-</span></b> ; aor. 1
		part.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπειλίξας</span> dub. in <i><span class="en">
			D.
			23.161
		</span></i> (iii p.lxxxviii Blass), but found in <i><span class="en">
			Gal.
			18(2).7
		</span></i>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>roll
			up</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μεταξὺ τοῦ βιβλίου</span>,
			i.e. <i>skip</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i> l. c.:—
				Med.
			, <i>wriggle behind one</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					220
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be rolled up</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπείλικτο ὥσπερ τὰ βιβλία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					4.26.8
				</span></i>
			.</div>
